urname>McCarron</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Foo</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>AWM</given-names></name><name><surname>Yip</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuo</surname><given-names>TT</given-names></name><name><surname>Pilch</surname><given-names>BZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wenig</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>EL</given-names></name><name><surname>Eveson</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Reichart</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sidransky</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nasopharyngeal carcinoma</article-title><source>Pathology and Genetics of Head and Neck Tumours World Health Organization Classification of Tumours</source><year>2005</year><publisher-loc>Lyon, France</publisher-loc><publisher-name>IARC Press</publisher-name><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>97</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>ET</given-names></name><name><surname>Adami</surname><given-names>H-O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The enigmatic epidemiology of nasopharyngeal carcinoma</article-title><source>Cancer Epidemiology, Biomarkers &#x00026; Prevention</source><year>2006</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>1765</fpage><lpage>1777</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cope</surname><given-names>JU</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A viral etiology for Ewing's sarcoma</article-title><source>Medical Hypotheses</source><year>2000</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>369</fpage><lpage>372